---
import ModuleWrapper, { type _ModuleWrapper, type _ModuleHeader } from "@/components/ui/modules/ModuleWrapper.astro";

export interface Props extends _ModuleWrapper {}

const props = Astro.props;

const header: _ModuleHeader = {
	...props.header,
	title: props.header?.title || "Learning and problem-solving",
};
---

<ModuleWrapper {...{ ...props, header }}>
	<h3 class="mb-3 text-lg">Curiosity-driven learning</h3>

	<p>
		I've always had an insatiable curiosity about how things work. I wanted to understand how people thought and behaved and how to influence positive change, so I became a coach. I found myself
		running a business for the first time, so I learnt what I could about sales, customer service and leadership. When I got curious about how websites work, that's when I started programming.
	</p>

	<p>When something interests me — something I can strive to master — I drive myself forward with a compulsion to learn as much as I can. That commitment is what gets me up a steep curve.</p>

	<p>
		<span class="text-bad">It can be draining</span>, though. I'm always pushing to the next level, looking for the next project to apply myself to. It makes me highly effective, and it can get
		chaotic.
	</p>

	<p>
		<strong>If I don't know how to do something, I can learn how.</strong> That simple philosophy is why I'm proficient across areas a traditional path might never have covered.
	</p>

	<hr class="my-8 border-line" />

	<h3 class="mb-3 text-lg">Solving problems</h3>

	<p>
		I have always loved solving problems, whether that's an issue as a coach, a digital solution for a customer, fixing a car or a woodworking project. There is always a logical reason you're
		facing a given challenge. Once I understand how it works, the obstacle disappears and the solution becomes clear.
	</p>

	<p>
		Defining the problem is the most important part, but doing the work to solve it is a different job — one that usually needs invention and a creative angle. As long as the end goal stays clear
		and properly defined, there are several ways to reach it.
	</p>

	<p class="font-semibold">My four steps to solving a problem</p>

	<ol class="ml-6 list-outside list-decimal space-y-1">
		<li><strong>Clearly define the problem.</strong> What is point A, the starting position.</li>
		<li><strong>Define a clear criteria for success.</strong> What is point B, and precisely what are you trying to achieve.</li>
		<li><strong>Understand the problem.</strong> Dig into what is causing the gap, step by step, to find the difference that makes the difference.</li>
		<li><strong>Implement a solution.</strong> Give it your best go, and if it doesn't meet the success criteria, return to step one and repeat.</li>
	</ol>
</ModuleWrapper>
